  "limitations": [
    "The execution ownership backend requires Linux/proc; unsupported platforms reject before launch. Direct domain validators remain available.",
    "Complete integration proof ran on an identical Linux filesystem checkout using Python3.12.3 and Node24.14.1. The Windows-mounted filesystem previously exceeded the unchanged300-second adapter limit; no mounted-filesystem broad success or performance guarantee is claimed.",
    "Hosted CI uses Python3.11 and Node24 and has not yet been observed. Local PR validation success is not hosted CI, merge or release completion.",
    "Historical failed prose and initial PR observations remain truthful evidence with specifically assessed replacement proof. Unrelated follow-ups and unmigrated contracts remain with their named owners."
  ],
  "outcome": "success",
  "rationale": [
    "All seven work entries are completed, all required reviews approved and every material finding resolved. Fresh independent validation-final-code-review assesses the complete diff and interactions; all139 exact subjects still match current bytes. Proposal, primary plan and12 registered models match current identities. The stale Validation registry hash was corrected through change.link to the exact already approved supplemental Design and final reviewed bytes; no Design body or decision changed.",
    "Required C1–C11 proof is complete and applicable: broad-smoke jobs1 and jobs2 each pass286 tasks including278 original cases and the complete38-test execution suite; CLI424, skill358, guide9, boundary reference28/validation90, adapter154, npm7 and release164 checks passed. Real sequential, individual and reversed parallel case populations agree. No required case or assertion was dropped.",
    "The actual PR wrapper passed against base57653f7b and source0d65cd67 with588 passed execution rows, including candidate preparation, preflight, selected and broad work. Subsequent commits contain only current initiative review/evidence/activity and the inspected model registration correction. Production, tests, specifications, models, dependencies and generated product inputs are byte-identical to that tested engineering basis. Fresh git diff --check and positional validate-change-metadata.py pass on current state.",
    "The initial actual PR failure remains recorded. Its two out-of-scope legacy navigation changes were restored byte-for-byte to main; the exact nine remaining grandfathered amendments have independent approved classification. Failed historical whole-file prose evidence remains failed; the final rename-aware comparison has12 retained baseline files and zero introduced findings. Approved retained-format scope and required plan/README gates support current reliance without a blanket waiver.",
    "Current canonical skill/resource and real package/release candidate proof establishes consumer coherence. No live publication, schema migration, historical store rewrite or broader customer adoption occurred. Process cleanup, invalid selector inputs, stale receipts, timeout/failure distinctions and retained negative/regression proof cover the changed security and failure boundaries. Exact source deletion and cache cleanup follow approved maps; unrelated responsibilities and files remain outside adoption.",
    "The branch is clean and governing artifacts tracked; remote main equals the normalized base and no remote branch was present. Review and Verify are distinct judgments. Successful Verify owns this final rationale; Route may close the initiative and the separately authorized PR skill may submit the branch."
  ],
